From 5e749449fedf32402d9a7da5de79a476b8642310 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:44:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add sync: trade the store with other devices through a drop
 zone

A drop zone is a directory every device can reach and nobody has to trust:
a local path, or sftp://user@host[:port][/dir]. Each device publishes one
file there, <device>.bundle.gpg: a git bundle of its whole history under the
single reference refs/pass-sync/<device>, signed with the device's OpenPGP
key (SHA-512) and encrypted to every device.

    pass sync setup device-name drop-zone own-key-fingerprint
    pass sync peer [--remove] device-name [key-fingerprint]
    pass sync push | fetch [device-name...]
    pass sync log | diff device-name
    pass sync merge device-name [--mine name | --theirs name]...

Receiving: a file is taken only when it decrypts to no more than 256 MiB,
carries one valid signature by the key configured for that device (not a
SHA-1 one), and holds that device's reference alone with its full history.
Its tip must be a synced store: entries, .gpg-id files and the .gitattributes
of "pass git init", nothing else; every .gpg-id line names a device, every
entry is encrypted to devices only. An older file served again is ignored.

Merging: devices are equals. An empty store adopts another's; a store with
nothing of its own moves forward; otherwise the two are merged, entry by
entry, following an entry that was moved (the same bytes, or the same text
when this device reads both). Where both sides did different things to one
entry, or to one folder's readers, nothing is taken until --mine or --theirs
says which stays. Then the entries that are not encrypted to the readers
their .gpg-id names, and that this device reads, are re-encrypted, and the
result is published.

The settings live in the store's git configuration (pass-sync.*); setup also
turns on signed commits. PASSWORD_STORE_GPG_OPTS applies to the gpg calls.

Also exit quietly when whoever reads the output goes away (| grep -q),
instead of a BrokenPipeError traceback.

Tests: u0008-sync-tests.sh, two stores and a directory between them.
